WEEK 1 | Commit 2

CHANGES:
- Fixed critical ForeignKeyViolation error in streaming chat endpoint
- Added LLM timeout handling with SSE error event emission
- Session ID now included in streaming done payload for frontend persistence

DETAILS:
- ROOT CAUSE: ChatSession row was only flushed (not committed) before StreamingResponse began
- Before: db.flush() only -> when message INSERT ran inside the streaming generator, it referenced
  a session_id that did not exist in the committed chat_sessions table -> ForeignKeyViolation crash
- After: Explicit db.commit() after session creation/resolution, before streaming response starts
- This was the #1 critical bug blocking the entire chat functionality from working
- Added asyncio.wait_for() with 90-second timeout for LLM API calls
- On timeout/failure: emits clean SSE error event so frontend stops spinner instead of hanging
- The done SSE payload now includes session_id so frontend can persist it to localStorage
- Streaming generator properly handles both successful completion and error paths

FILES: backend/app/routers/chat_stream.py
